  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies gate-based quantum multiple kernel learning (QMKL) for financial binary classification on HSBC digital payment fraud, German Credit, and Bank Marketing datasets, using fidelity and projected quantum kernels with 4-20 feature/qubit dimensions. On simulator, quantum MKL is often competitive and sometimes best (notably PQ-MKL AVE on HSBC), while on IBM ibm_auckland hardware the authors show that error mitigation substantially improves kernel fidelity, with projected kernels reaching r2 values up to 0.984 at 12 qubits and 0.926 at 16 qubits.",
